From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] avcodec/h264dec: export AV_FRAME_DATA_VIDEO_BLOCK_PARAMS

Add AV_CODEC_EXPORT_DATA_VIDEO_BLOCK_PARAMS ("block_params" in
export_side_data). When it is set, the h264 decoder records the
macroblock-layer syntax of every decoded macroblock while parsing (CAVLC,
CABAC and skipped macroblocks, MBAFF and field pictures included) into a
per-picture pool table, and attaches one AVH264MacroblockParams per
macroblock to each output frame: mb_type class, sub_mb_type, reference
indices and prediction direction per 8x8 partition, intra 4x4/8x8/16x16 and
chroma prediction modes as signalled, coded_block_pattern, mb_qp_delta,
transform_size_8x8_flag, mb_field_decoding_flag, slice index and the motion
vector differences of both lists.

Nothing is recorded or allocated when the flag is unset, and hwaccel
decoding never exports. With frame threading the export waits for the
picture's decoding progress, so droppable pictures report progress while
the flag is set. Decoded pixels are unchanged.

tools/vblock_data_dump prints the side data, and the new
fate-h264-block-params-* tests cover CAVLC, CABAC, MBAFF and CABAC with
frame threads (which must match the single-threaded reference).

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to ffmpeg-devel by OVT WI-4.103]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Rationale: FFmpeg's h264 decoder exports MVs and per-MB QP only; Open Video
  Tools needs mb_type, sub_mb_type, ref_idx, intra modes, cbp, mb_qp_delta
  and mvd (OVT spec chapter 07 section 7.6.3). Part 2 of 2 (OVT WI-4.101);
  part 1 (libavutil side data) is OVT WI-4.100.
